{{- /*
The title, with how many are left beside it.

It was a row of its own under the price, which put a fact about whether you
can have this thing three paragraphs away from the thing. Beside the title it
is read in the same glance as the name, boxed like the unavailable panel
below so the two read as the same kind of remark about the same product.

Nothing at all when there are none left: the panel underneath is already
saying that, and "0 left" beside "Currently unavailable" is the page saying
it twice.
*/ -}}
{{ if stockLeft . }}--steps[chip={{ stockLeft . }}, chipink=quoteBar]--
{{ .Title }}
--/steps--
{{ else }}# {{ .Title }}
{{ end }}

{{- /*
Said once.

This was a panel with the words written in it and the same words pinned to
its corner as a ribbon, which drew them on top of each other. The ribbon is
for a card on the shop front, where there is no room to explain: here there
is room, so the panel says what it is and why.
*/}}
{{ if unavailable . }}
--panel[padding=14, margin=0 0 12 0, border=1, color=quoteBar, radius=8]--
**{{ soldOutLabel }}**

{{ unavailableSays . }}
--/panel--
{{ end }}
{{ with productImage .Image }}![]({{.}})

{{ end -}}
Tags: {{ .Tags }}

{{ .Description }}

**{{ money .Price }}**{{ with dcr .Price }}
≈ {{.}} at today's rate. The amount you pay is set when you order.{{ end }}

---
{{ if unavailable . }}
{{- /*
No way to add it, rather than a button that refuses.

The card said the shop could not sell this and the button was still here,
which is the worst of both: somebody who presses it has been told no and
shown a way round it.
*/}}
[Back to the shop]({{storeIndex}})
{{ else }}
## Add to Cart
--form--
type="action" value="/addToCart"
type="hidden" name="sku" value="{{.SKU}}"
type="intinput" label="Quantity" name="qty" value="1"
type="submit" label="Add To Cart"
--/form--
{{ end }}
